      {
        "block_id": "T9B4dyG55oh4TNxOlTNcm6qNncd",
        "block_type": 4,
        "heading2": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "How encryption works",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        },
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "KHoidKDk9ogHOex7ZuUcqrpgngh",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "On Zilliz Cloud, a customer-managed encryption key is a cryptographic key created by your cloud provider's KMS and used to secure data in your clusters. After adding your KMS key to a Zilliz Cloud Business Critical project, you can use it to encrypt data stored on disk, in object storage, and in message queues.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "Fg4jd6cq1oC6BpxlqMFcCYd3nGd",
        "block_type": 43,
        "board": {
          "token": "Ehcyw7EZphWQO0bTJMDchzTYnIf"
        },
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "YLZ9dH4t9oJhy5xOZd1c986DnCf",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "As shown in the diagram above, Zilliz Cloud manages encryption keys hierarchically, using the user-supplied KMS key as the ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "root key",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": ". ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "AWvld8OnQo3m8DxLq5tcxOhjnFb",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Within a cluster, each database is associated with an ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Encryption Zone (EZ)",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": ", and Zilliz Cloud creates an encryption key for each zone, known as an ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Encryption Zone Key (EZK)",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": ". To protect the EZKs, Zilliz Cloud encrypts them using the root key and stores the encrypted EZKs.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "M84edH6v7ovEbZx5WjVcEW51nxg",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "For each database file, Zilliz Cloud generates a ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Data Encryption Key (DEK)",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": " and uses it to encrypt the file. To secure the DEK, Zilliz Cloud encrypts it with the EZK and stores both the encrypted DEK and the encrypted files.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "CvwQdsKcAouEDrxg38McoLbNnff",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "When accessing a file, Zilliz Cloud sends the encrypted EZK to the KMS for decryption, uses the decrypted EZK to decrypt the encrypted DEK, and uses the decrypted DEK to decrypt the file.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "Z5n7dEPsUoDRaVxXbMncyNKMnV3",
        "block_type": 4,
        "heading2": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Encryption scope",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        },
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "HMXNdNvjSoSNdaxpwImcAP83nYg",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "All data-related files stored in the following locations are encrypted:",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "KuU4dVKw0oVqm7xjGHicg33lnwe",
        "block_type": 12,
        "bullet": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Object storage, including binlogs and index files,",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        },
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "OgEFdTZKpo2xwmxLONgcdcjenOd",
        "block_type": 12,
        "bullet": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Local disk, and ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        },
        "parent_id": "QHPsdJ4UkoxpdTxt6S1clHqsnuf"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "RghbdG4NXon2Z1xwYY5cEewRnOb",
        "block_type": 12,
        "bullet": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Insert/delete messages in message queues.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
